What effects the accuracy of a wand of death?

I always use a wand of death on the Wizard.  Until my last game,
it usually got him first zap, and second at the latest.  In the
last game, however, when I woke him up, it kept missing until he
got next to me (about 4 shots, I think), at which point, he
stole my Sceptre of Might, making further shots with the wand
useless, although I didn't realize it at first.  (He then double
troubled, and then generated a swarm of monsters.  Including
(ha, ha) a cockatrice which left a corpse.)

In all further encounters with him (and it seems like there were
a lot more than usual), the wand of death did the trick first
shot, so I'm wondering if there was something which affected its
accuracy before.  Preferably something I can avoid in the
future.

